    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323-a1">

                <pb facs="0466" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg378"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 165.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Count Vorontzoff Daschkoff to Mr. Smith</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministre de la Maison de l’Empereur</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1892-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                                1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: His Majesty the Emperor presents to R. W.
                    Sargent, captain of the <hi rendition="#italic">Indiana</hi>, an enameled goblet
                    in remembrance of the part he took in bringing the flour offered by the citizens
                    of Philadelphia to our people suffering from want of bread. Would you he so Mud
                    as to transfer it to its destination and receive,</p>
                <p>Sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ct. Vorontzoff
                    Daschkoff</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
